# The real Firebase config. config.example.js is the committed template; copy it to
# config.js and fill it in. Kept out of git not because these values are secret -- a
# Firebase web API key is a public identifier -- but because the file is per-checkout
# and a committed copy would be silently stale for the next person.
# Anchored: only the per-checkout secret at this directory's root. lib/config.js is the
# committed loader that reads it and must stay tracked — a bare `config.js` pattern
# would match at any depth and silently drop the loader too.
/config.js
